---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';
import { BOOK } from '../../press';

// Deliberately a forthcoming listing: no manuscript, no excerpt, no sample
// chapter. See src/press.ts for why.
---

<Base
  title="Artistic Intelligence: A Manifesto"
  description="Josh Penzell's forthcoming book — a theater director's way of seeing, applied to work and to AI. Join the list to hear when it is out."
  path="/press/artistic-intelligence/"
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">{BOOK.status} · Imagination Applied Press</p>
    <h1>{BOOK.title}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{BOOK.subtitle}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap page-body">
    <p class="pull">{BOOK.premise}</p>

    <p>
      AI made generation cheap. It did not make judgment cheap. When anyone can produce a
      plausible answer in seconds, the scarce thing stops being production and starts
      being taste—knowing which of the plausible answers is worth having, and being able
      to say why.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a book about where that judgment comes from. It argues that the people who
      have spent their lives making things under uncertainty—directors, designers,
      writers, anyone who has had to commit to an interpretation before the evidence was
      in—have been practising the exact capacity the rest of us now need.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is a way of seeing rather than a method. The practice built on top of it,
      TheaterThink, is a separate project and a separate book.
    </p>

    <div class="section-rule">
      <h2>Hear when it is out</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        One email when the book is available. Nothing else, and no list sharing.
      </p>

      <form class="form" method="POST" action="/api/waitlist" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <input type="hidden" name="list" value="artistic-intelligence" />
        <div class="field">
          <label for="email">Email</label>
          <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" />
        </div>
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label for="company_website">Do not fill this in</label>
          <input id="company_website" name="company_website" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>
        <button class="btn" type="submit">Join the list</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="section-rule">
      <h2>About the author</h2>
      <p>
        Josh Penzell is a keynote speaker, advisor, and founder of Imagination Applied. A
        theater director turned AI strategist, he helps leaders create direction when the
        answer is not waiting to be found—aligning people, directing AI, and rehearsing
        what comes next.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={SITE.founderSite}>joshpenzell.com</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/press/">More from the Press</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
